                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "46f0fc71-e6b8-3d62-aee3-7b31e0586c72",
                        "entry_id": "ddb60fe7-76f6-3e6f-b5e5-e20ff0a8f1a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. свойство по значению прилагательного многовариантный; наличие или возможность множества вариантов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a593c8f4-8204-43b0-a780-b9fd3ab7baf0",
                                "sense_id": "46f0fc71-e6b8-3d62-aee3-7b31e0586c72",
                                "text": "Распад гетерокарионов с автономными ядрами обеспечивает многовариантность разновидностей, форм, штаммов, с помощью которых дейтеромицеты распространяются и захватывают новые ареалы и экологические ниши."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "92c5db97-03dd-41b9-8869-426d8b0c28e8",
                        "source_entry_id": "ddb60fe7-76f6-3e6f-b5e5-e20ff0a8f1a5",
                        "source_sense_id": "46f0fc71-e6b8-3d62-aee3-7b31e0586c72",
                        "target_lang_word": "diversity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diversity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f57660a-155e-322b-8cc2-67fafba19a80",
                                        "entry_id": "dbc42af8-67ac-3217-b75a-77c372c33597",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being diverse or different; difference or unlikeness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b596dd8-f697-4f87-964e-881dbbbdd55b",
                                                "sense_id": "0f57660a-155e-322b-8cc2-67fafba19a80",
                                                "text": "From this view of the case, my friends, I am driven irresistibly to the conclusion that diversity, dissimilarity, variety in all our local and domestic institutions, is the great safeguard of our liberties"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b423f501-4b0d-4949-850a-ace2a7b0d24c",
                                                "sense_id": "0f57660a-155e-322b-8cc2-67fafba19a80",
                                                "text": "On December 17 I addressed the UN General Assembly, stating that it was this nation's policy to help create a world that \"can be safe for diversity and free from hostility.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60c75111-8796-4438-afe1-63d842fe50a4",
                                                "sense_id": "0f57660a-155e-322b-8cc2-67fafba19a80",
                                                "text": "One place there were none, of course, was on the Buckingham Palace balcony, as was observed by the Bridgerton actor Adjoa Andoh – who contrasted on the ITV coverage “the rich diversity of the abbey” and “a terribly white balcony”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9aece4d-ab42-3d50-b1a9-50acf8051e99",
                                        "entry_id": "dbc42af8-67ac-3217-b75a-77c372c33597",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A variety; diverse types or examples."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73ba2adf-92ef-4d99-840e-0df5c2737195",
                                                "sense_id": "d9aece4d-ab42-3d50-b1a9-50acf8051e99",
                                                "text": "Hendryx has laid down eight tracks that flow seamlessly through funk, disco, gospel, rock and reggae, with nary a false step along the way. She is at home in this diversity of styles because she has paid her dues in all of them: from her days as one of the dynamoes of Labelle through collaborations with rock band Talking Heads, funk band Cameo […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf7afd78-74c2-407c-9b63-446e9b22c036",
                                                "sense_id": "d9aece4d-ab42-3d50-b1a9-50acf8051e99",
                                                "text": "The San Juan market is Mexico City's most famous deli of exotic meats, where an adventurous shopper can hunt down hard-to-find critters such as ostrich, wild boar and crocodile. Only the city zoo offers greater species diversity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9577ed3f-e3b6-3aba-9ea6-d73a7a26e737",
                                        "entry_id": "dbc42af8-67ac-3217-b75a-77c372c33597",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Equal-opportunity inclusion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4324c69a-4a9a-40ea-8383-3e1420e4b38e",
                                                "sense_id": "9577ed3f-e3b6-3aba-9ea6-d73a7a26e737",
                                                "text": "Bakke has shaped a precarious context for diversity initiatives in higher education. On the one hand, the U.S. Supreme Court has reasoned that race may serve a purpose in the admissions process; however, race may not be used as a corrective measure, such as by establishing quotas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a88ab044-9507-4685-840c-f47868ea68db",
                                                "sense_id": "9577ed3f-e3b6-3aba-9ea6-d73a7a26e737",
                                                "text": "Diversity is now a big industry — about $8 billion per year gets spent on diversity trainings in America — and parents might be feeling blindsided by the rapid changes, many of which came after last year’s George Floyd protests."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "760ff05d-6b97-47aa-9c27-5e823126db1b",
                        "source_entry_id": "ddb60fe7-76f6-3e6f-b5e5-e20ff0a8f1a5",
                        "source_sense_id": "46f0fc71-e6b8-3d62-aee3-7b31e0586c72",
                        "target_lang_word": "alternation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alternation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ef51695-1e39-3a52-b3ba-4ca8fac50c93",
                                        "entry_id": "6a92050f-5d39-3ad4-b561-20a939f6eec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The reciprocal succession of (normally two) things in time or place; the act of following and being followed by turns; alternate succession, performance, or occurrence"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f59678ca-8bf0-40d2-a4c3-f24b1e39f03b",
                                                "sense_id": "7ef51695-1e39-3a52-b3ba-4ca8fac50c93",
                                                "text": "the alternation of day and night"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b135a67-7788-40c7-b91e-e1a9709e8415",
                                                "sense_id": "7ef51695-1e39-3a52-b3ba-4ca8fac50c93",
                                                "text": "alternation of summer and winter"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97a47e77-224c-4752-922e-eec30b35d618",
                                                "sense_id": "7ef51695-1e39-3a52-b3ba-4ca8fac50c93",
                                                "text": "alternation between night shifts and day shifts"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f756d1d0-8a8a-40bc-8d5d-603be9f70be7",
                                                "sense_id": "7ef51695-1e39-3a52-b3ba-4ca8fac50c93",
                                                "text": "alternation of feelings between hope and fear"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b303bf1-8887-3ce1-90b1-9f5dff98f734",
                                        "entry_id": "6a92050f-5d39-3ad4-b561-20a939f6eec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The response of the congregation speaking alternately with the minister."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0aafba47-073c-45ba-8165-1067df0501c6",
                                                "sense_id": "0b303bf1-8887-3ce1-90b1-9f5dff98f734",
                                                "text": "There are Anthems to be found amongst them , where every syllable has its just length ; each part of a sentence its proper pause : where the words are not confused by perplexing alternations, or rendered tedious by unnecessary repetitions"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a9028a5-156d-3ea6-b50c-a4a315c08339",
                                        "entry_id": "6a92050f-5d39-3ad4-b561-20a939f6eec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ablaut."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20ec92c3-6343-34dc-8e11-06c4d218f4fc",
                                        "entry_id": "6a92050f-5d39-3ad4-b561-20a939f6eec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pattern by which more than one construct is possible, as with \\\"Alice cooked Bob dinner\\\" and \\\"Alice cooked dinner for Bob\\\"."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
