                                        "entry_id": "6a92050f-5d39-3ad4-b561-20a939f6eec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of partial truncation of a polygon, polyhedron or tiling in which alternate vertices are removed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5206136f-1884-471b-bbf2-fe62e3b2047f",
                                                "sense_id": "42282ba7-bb4e-3a9c-8bb5-2bd695458045",
                                                "text": "1932, Harold Scott Macdonald Coxeter, The densities of the regular polytopes, part 2, reprinted in 1995, F. Arthur Sherk, Peter Mcmullen, Anthony C. Thompson, Asia Ivić Weiss (editors), Kaleidoscopes: Selected Writings of H. S. M. Coxeter, page 54,\nThis case suggests that the alternation of a polyhedron should be bounded by actual vertex figures and alternated faces. The case of the cube is in agreement with this notion, since the alternated square is nothing."
                                            }
